    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1fa443e4-4658-550d-8cea-40c80f0f1123",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that by replacing $a_{33}$ and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. The other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form.",
